 "notes": "Top-down pinch grasp with a regrasp fallback. In init the controller reads the target cube's pose and tries the four hand yaws that line up with the cube's faces (cube yaw + k\u00b790\u00b0). For each it solves damped-least-squares IK, with a null-space term that keeps joints away from their limits, for a pose 14 cm above the cube and for the grasp pose. It drops yaws that don't solve or sit near joint limits. Among the rest it picks the one whose hand footprint (thumb behind, fingers ahead) is furthest from the other cubes, with a mild preference for a yaw near the home direction.\n\nMotion sequence:\n- Smooth joint-space move to the pre-grasp pose.\n- Straight-line moves along / down to the grasp point (site 5 mm above the cube centre).\n- Closing: fingers 0.2\u21920.5 over 0.5 s, then thumb 0.5\u21921 over 0.4 s. While closing, an integral correction holds the measured grasp site in place, because when the arm is stretched out the fingers push the hand up and forward and the cube was otherwise squeezed out.\n- Lift to 17.5 cm. If the cube didn't come up with the hand, it opens, raises and re-plans.\n- Before transport it picks the yaw above the bin for which both the carry pose and the low place pose (\u00b13 cm) solve with the palm facing down. Transport is a joint-space move.\n- During transport, if the cube drops away from the hand, it opens, raises and re-plans.\n- Lowering corrects for where the cube actually sits in the hand. The cube is set down almost touching the bin floor.\n- Release is slow: thumb opens over 0.6 s, fingers over 1.5 s.\n- The open hand is then re-centred over the cube and rises slowly. If the cube starts rising with it, the hand goes back down, re-centres and tries again (up to 4 times).\n\nResults: 40/40 on each of the last two batches, 120 different seeds (100000\u2013100039 and 100114\u2013100153). Earlier versions failed on things since fixed: cube flung on release, dragged out of the bin on retreat, IK getting stuck, and far grasps failing.\n\nKnown weaknesses:\n- **Far-reach grasps (x \u2248 0.25\u20130.31) are marginal.** The closing correction hits its \u00b13 cm / \u22124 cm limits there and the hand still ends up about 2 cm high. Seed 100006 needed one regrasp.\n- **Some lucky successes.** In at least seed 100114, and probably 100039, the cube seems to have slipped out of the hand on the way and landed in the bin anyway.\n- **Placement is loose.** Final cube positions vary by about \u00b13 cm from the bin centre, and a few cubes end up slightly tilted against a wall.\n- **Neighbouring cubes** are sometimes nudged by 1\u20133 cm during the grasp, but none was pushed into a bin in testing.\n- **Slower than it needs to be.** Most successes finish around 10\u201312 s; the worst I saw was 23.2 s after two regrasps, close to the 25 s limit.\n- Two debug `print` statements are still in the code; they don't affect behaviour.",
